  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "fashion-lapel-jacket",
      "topicId": "fashion",
      "sourceOrder": 41,
      "cycle": 0,
      "status": "READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "Как называется отогнутая наружу часть переднего борта пиджака, обычно продолжающая воротник?",
            "answers": [
              "Вытачка",
              "Ластовица",
              "Лацкан",
              "Складка"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 2
          },
          "literalSHA256": "851a8ec4271c40b4ebef7006353719785cd99ad2190dc28ac3476814ed929653",
          "primaryGround": "The prompt asks for a turned-back front part of a jacket that normally continues the collar (lapel L38-L40). The three other labels are garment-construction terms with distinct definitions: a stitched tapering fold (dart L69-L74), a seam insert for expansion/reinforcement (gusset L38-L40), and a doubled cloth fold (pleat L62-L65).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view0:L31-L40;L62-L68; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view1:L69-L74; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view2:L31-L40; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view3:L60-L65",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "Лацкан — отогнутая часть переда пальто или пиджака, обычно являющаяся продолжением воротника. Вытачка — застроченный сужающийся сгиб, ластовица — вставка в шве для расширения или укрепления, а складка — перегиб ткани, образованный удвоением материала.",
          "literalSHA256": "3247394f2ae0c7b901fb8a746dcf555cf9f45f630c282cd739929dcfe5f1d555",
          "primaryGround": "Each clause restates the respective dictionary definition and distinguishes the front-of-coat fold from seam shaping, a seam insert, and a doubled fabric fold.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view0:L31-L40;L62-L68; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view1:L69-L74; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view2:L31-L40; /originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view3:L60-L65",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Вытачка — застроченный сужающийся сгиб в одежде.",
          "literalSHA256": "94254768affc3dfc7b5810e370361ddfcef651a987f556e90ae67651bdddedf5",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines the garment sense of dart as a stitched tapering fold.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view1:L69-L74",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note1",
          "literal": "Ластовица — обычно треугольная или ромбовидная вставка в шве; она увеличивает ширину или укрепляет одежду.",
          "literalSHA256": "744def13915dfb28ace6bbf542c2ea69d4029ec0001a0b01115022a3f874789e",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines a gusset as a usually triangular or diamond-shaped insert in a seam that provides expansion or reinforcement.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view2:L31-L40",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note2",
          "literal": "Лацкан — отогнутая часть переда пальто, обычно продолжающая воротник; первое известное употребление lapel датировано 1789 годом.",
          "literalSHA256": "fa254b5bd894993af65806b846533983efb07c24888d7b5ce6cd8eb544418b1e",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines lapel as the turned-back part of a garment, specifically a coat-front fold usually continuing the collar; its first-known-use date is 1789.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view0:L31-L40;L62-L68",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note3",
          "literal": "Складка — перегиб ткани, образованный складыванием материала поверх самого себя.",
          "literalSHA256": "3eebd6782fd82193212ca1815e95b6591ed45b6d0d241a3524abb81d68f1a497",
          "primaryGround": "Merriam-Webster defines a pleat as a fold in cloth made by doubling material over on itself.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ],
          "locator": "/originalRecord/payload/output/1/text#turn0view3:L60-L65",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a17c8c/source-fashion41/merriam-webster-fashion-terms.json"
          ]
